INT. PARKING GARAGE STAIRWELL - NIGHT

Concrete. Flickering tube light. A door slams two floors below.

LOTTE VANTERPOOL (30s, trench coat, press badge) freezes mid-step. Phone in hand.

Footsteps. Climbing. Fast.

She jabs the screen. Voice memo.

LOTTE (V.O.)
(recording, calm)
If you hear this, I'm already in the stairwell of Level B. The ledger is in the glovebox of the grey Fiat.

She kills it. Backs up. Hits the rail. Whispers.

LOTTE
Come on, come on.

The footsteps stop. Right below her. Waiting.

She doesn't breathe. A key jingles. Then a little girl's laugh echoes up. A father's voice, humming.

They pass. Door opens. Closes. Gone.

Lotte slides down the wall. Laughs. Wipes her eyes.

LOTTE (CONT'D)
Idiot.

She replays the memo. Deletes it. Stands. Walks on.
